														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4216440">
									

<p>I see what you mean. The central conceit here is that it’s a fun little curiosity with a horrifying twist ending, but until the twist hits all you’ve really got is “fun little curiosity”. It's designed to lull you into a false sense of security, but boring by design is still boring&#8230;</p>
<p>I can't imagine that heavier foreshadowing of the ending would help, though. O5 overreactions are a staple of poorly thought out newbie articles: I certainly don’t want to make it look like one of those.</p>
<p>If I can come up with a good idea for an early hook I may yet take the whole thing back to the sandbox, but for now I'll leave it up and see whether other people have the same problem with it you did.</p>

							</div>

								
