<p>I think use of redactions is more down to preference and what your personal headcanon is as to why the Foundation database is available on a creative writing site. Since other articles have the user inputting O5 credentials and reading all the Things Too Terrifying For Humanity To Know, I personally don’t see the point in redacting much at all in these articles. I use it here primarily for pacing (“redacted for brevity”).</p>
<p>The audio logs are transcripts of the “high pitched sound” emitted by the object every time it creates a paradox. The sound itself has to be artificially slowed down and pitched in an audible range, otherwise it just sounds like a squeak.</p>

