<p>That's why they didn't figure it out the first time.</p>
<p>The second time, they remembered having successfully duplicated an object once, wondered why the same thing hadn't happened then &#8212; and then realized maybe it <em>had</em>. That noise/air-puff only happened during paradox tests, after all&#8230;</p>
<p>I admit that it's still quite a leap. But not unimaginable, IMO, especially from someone who's worked with parallel/split universes/timelines/what-have-you. (I doubt the currency-duplicating guy every figured it out, any of the many times he found himself being smothered by/turning into his ill-gotten gains&#8230;)</p>

